<title>USA: Vermont's biggest hospital plans cost reductions.</title>
<headline>Vermont's biggest hospital plans cost reductions.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Board of Trustees for Vermont's largest hospital, Fletcher Allen Health Care, announced plans to cut operating expenses by about $17 million over the next two years.</p>
<p>This will include 425 full-time jobs, with the reductions achieved through attrition, retraining, re-assignment, early retirement and a voluntary separation program.</p>
<p>Chief Executive Officer, Doctor John Frymoyer, said medical care at Fletcher Allen is &quot;too expensive&quot; and that other hospitals provide the same service with fewer staff.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
